                <head>EC–14. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>In a memorandum of conversation with Assistant Secretary of State Roy R.
                    Rubottom, Jr., on March 14, 1960, Ambassador José R. Chiriboga Villagómez
                    referred to a recent Ecuadoran request for a sugar quota of 35,000 tons in 1960.
                    Assistant Secretary Rubottom replied that the problem was under study.
                    (822.235/3–1460) In a note of July 21, 1960, to Ambassador Ravndal, Foreign
                    Minister Tobar raised the Ecuadoran request to a 40,000 ton sugar quota in the
                    fourth quarter of 1960. (822.235/7–2660) The Secretary of State informed
                    Ambassador Chiriboga in a note dated August 5, 1960, that the United States
                    could not consider Ecuador as a source of sugar in the reassignment of Cuba’s
                    quota for 1960. (822.235/7–1160)</p>
            </div>
